      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/ef9202db6a03e38951fec2342da76330ca837d21/vllm%2Fmodels%2Fkimi_k3%2Famd%2Fspecialized_decode%2FREADME.md",
      "changes": 3,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/vllm%2Fmodels%2Fkimi_k3%2Famd%2Fspecialized_decode%2FREADME.md?ref=ef9202db6a03e38951fec2342da76330ca837d21",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "vllm/models/kimi_k3/amd/specialized_decode/README.md",
      "patch": "@@ -55,7 +55,8 @@ AITER MXFP4 bmms (`VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FP4BMM=1`). Without them the MLA layers\n run vLLM's attention ops, then K2, and startup logs why; DCP1 runs only with M1\n and is refused. The KDA layers run K1 and K2 either way.\n \n-KV transfer support is limited to built-in MoRIIO READ and WRITE consumers.\n+KV transfer support is limited to built-in MoRIIO READ and WRITE consumers and\n+the built-in Mooncake consumer.\n Keep the producer on `decode_backend=auto` and use matching cache layouts.\n \n If you request the specialized decode for anything else, startup fails with one",
